<title>UK: Russia's Novorossiisk oil port reopens for loading.</title>
<headline>Russia's Novorossiisk oil port reopens for loading.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's Black Sea port of Novorossiisk reopened in the early hours of Thursday morning after being closed due to bad weather since 21l0 GMT Tuesday, a shipping inspector said.</p>
<p>They said that no ships had been loaded in the last 24 hours.</p>
<p>-- Colin Wooster, London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7456</p>
